    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. Can I Eat Whatever I Want During Invisalign Treatment, Like I Could Not With Traditional Braces? Yes. Unlike traditional braces with metal brackets, Invisalign aligners are removable, so you can enjoy any food choices as long as you remove the Invisalign trays before eating and store them safely. 2. Can I Drink Coffee or Other Beverages While Wearing Invisalign Clear Aligners? The only beverage allowed while wearing Invisalign aligners is plain water. Orthodontic specialists advise removing trays before you drink coffee or other beverages to prevent staining, tooth decay, and gum disease. 3. What is the Simple Rule I Should Follow Before and After Meals With Invisalign Trays? The simple rule is to remove Invisalign trays before eating or drinking anything except water. After meals, brush your teeth and rinse the aligners to prevent food particles from being trapped under the trays. 4. How Do I Prevent Food Particles and Gum Disease While Wearing Invisalign Aligners? Dental specialists recommend brushing your teeth after eating and before putting Invisalign trays back in. Rinsing your mouth and aligners helps prevent food particles, bacteria buildup, and gum disease while protecting your beautiful smile. 5. What Should I Do With My Invisalign Trays During Special Occasions or When Eating Out? Orthodontists advise removing Invisalign clear aligners before meals and placing them in a protective case, not in a napkin or spinner white decorative wrap. Carry a travel toothbrush so consistent habits protect your treatment and avoid costly tray damage."
    }
